Original commit body from d4edf00:

Bytes literals (like b'hello') are now serialized as their repr() string
instead of causing TypeError during JSON serialization. This is a follow-up
to the complex number fix - tensorflow also contains bytes literals.

Both non-JSON-serializable types are now handled:
- Complex numbers (1+2j) -> "(1+2j)"
- Bytes literals (b'hello') -> "b'hello'"
